    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d167">

                <pb facs="0510" n="473" xml:id="pg473"/>

                <head>167. Telegram From the Department of State to the Embassy in Iran<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d167-f1"/>
                </head>
                <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                    <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                        when="1953-02-28T18:50:00-05:00">February 28, 1953, 6:50 p.m.</date>
                </dateline>
                <p>2254. Dept completely concurs your decision take energetic measures discourage
                    Shah’s departure (Urtel 3449 rptd London 1124),<anchor n="2" xml:id="d167-f2"/>
                    believing that risk involved was worth taking in fluid situation. Deptel 2238
                    rptd London 5752<anchor n="3" xml:id="d167-f3"/> was not rpt not intended
                    discourage you from taking such action, but, since we then unable foresee
                    circumstances where intervention could be useful (Urtel 3397 rptd London
                        1103),<anchor n="4" xml:id="d167-f4"/> only to assure you that inactivity in
                    crisis would be understood here.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>Dulles</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
